vLLM #65283 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65283; first #63351), backported to v0.32.0, on #65282.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.32.0 (5df63a720):

  8875d37d3 [Core] Priority scheduling: hold lower-priority prefill for first tokens (cherry-picked from 20af4e098)
    Backport: v0.32.0's request queues stay stock, so the queue method is
    the scheduler's _has_lower_priority_than here, with the same answer; and
    v0.32.0's SchedulerStats and Prometheus logger have no field for the budget
    cap's holds, so the scheduler counts them and make_stats leaves them.

